Key Takeaways

Follina (CVE-2022-30190) abuses the Microsoft Support Diagnostic Tool (msdt.exe) via a malicious Word document.
No macro is required – the exploit uses an external HTML reference.
Simple parent-child process monitoring (winword.exe → msdt.exe) is an effective detection method.
Always analyse Office documents as ZIP archives to inspect relationships and external links.
VirusTotal + public research reports are enough to fully solve this Easy IR challenge.



